+---
+id: dl-005-generate-granular-structural-json-patches
+type: decision-log
+title: "Generate granular structural JSON Patches"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Clients need RFC 6902 patch documents that send local changes rather than replacing the entire JSON
+document. The existing library validates JSON values and does not mutate supplied inputs.
+
+## Decision
+
+Generate patches structurally: recurse through object members, emitting removals before replacements
+and additions; use escaped RFC 6901 pointer tokens; and compare arrays from their shared prefix and
+suffix so insertions and removals are expressed as indexed operations. Replace a value only when its
+JSON type or scalar value changes. Clone every operation value.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Small changes to object members and contiguous array regions remain small patches, while values that
+cannot be safely decomposed are replaced at their own path. The generator remains deterministic and
+does not mutate or share mutable values with either input.
